LC8 (#875) — Dev runs explorer (UI)

Adds a dev-run renderer to the existing runs explorer so `domain: 'code'`
execution_tasks render their diff, build log, test output, PR status,
Actions URL, and drift report. AI-run rendering is untouched; the
selector branches purely on `domain`.

Changes:
- New component `src/components/admin/DevRunDetail.tsx` rendering
  Diff (via existing TextDiffView), Build log, Test output, Drift
  report, PR status badge, View PR + Replay actions, error panel,
  held-for-review banner that deep-links to /admin/approvals.
- `agents-repo.listAgentRunsRich` now selects `pr_url`,
  `external_run_url`, `runner` and surfaces optional dev fields
  (`dev_diff`, `dev_build_log`, `dev_test_output`, `dev_drift`,
  `dev_logs`, `pr_url`, `external_run_url`, `pr_status`, raw
  `payload`) on the rich row. Reads execution_result with several
  fallback key names because LC1-7 backend is still out of scope.
- Wired the renderer switch in BOTH the legacy
  `src/pages/admin/AdminAgentRunsPage.tsx` (relevant file in the
  task) and the canonical `src/pages/admin/control/runs/RunsExplorer.tsx`
  (the `/admin/control` shell mentioned by the task). AdminAgentRunsPage
  also gains the existing `ReplayDialog` so its Replay button goes
  through the canonical `taskDispatcher` (no direct builder call).
- Test: `src/components/admin/__tests__/DevRunDetail.test.tsx`
  (8 cases) — sections render, View PR is an external link to
  pr_url, Replay fires onReplay, fallback to logs[] when build_log
  empty, drift section hidden when missing, held-for-review deep
  link to approvals.

All 8 component tests pass. Type-check clean for changed files.
ESLint reports one pre-existing error in agents-repo.ts:13
(direct supabase client import) that existed before this task.

